\begin_layout Standard
Four possible causes were examined:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Digitization.
\series default
 The random click error is 
\begin_inset Formula $\pm0.14$
\end_inset
 to 
\begin_inset Formula $\pm0.32\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
. The vertical axis of the hand-drawn figure is not evenly spaced, which makes the two-point calibration read values up to 
\begin_inset Formula $1.6\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
 too negative. Both are an order of magnitude smaller than the differences.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
The applied field.
\series default
 It enters only through 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{B}$
\end_inset
. Sweeping 
\begin_inset Formula $\theta_{B}$
\end_inset
 from 
\begin_inset Formula $60^{\circ}$
\end_inset
 to 
\begin_inset Formula $130^{\circ}$
\end_inset
 shows that no single angle fits all curves, and the angles that fit better would need a negative applied field at the streamer head.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
The unreported parameters.
\series default
 A least-squares fit with 
