\begin_layout Subsubsection
The Second Corona Streamer
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The paper gives the first inception as a voltage, not a field. At that instant there is no space charge yet, so the inception field at the tip is the applied field alone:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
E_{inc}=E_{ex}(0)\big|_{V=27.5\,\text{kV}}=149.37\,\text{kV/cm}.\label{eq:repro_inception_field}
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The tip geometry and the gas do not change after the first streamer, so a second streamer is assumed to start when the total tip field returns to this value:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
V(t)\,e_{ex}(0)+E_{sp}\left(0;z_{\text{drift}}(t)\right)+E_{I_{rod}}\left(0;z_{\text{drift}}(t)\right)+E_{I_{plane}}\left(0;z_{\text{drift}}(t)\right)\ge E_{inc},\label{eq:repro_second_streamer}
\end{equation}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where 
\begin_inset Formula $e_{ex}(0)$
\end_inset
 is the applied field at the tip for 
\begin_inset Formula $1\,\text{V}$
\end_inset
. The criterion 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{c}=5\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
 is not used here: it is the field a streamer needs to keep propagating, applied at the streamer head, whereas starting a new streamer at the tip requires ionization, i.e. roughly 
\begin_inset Formula $25$
\end_inset
 to 
\begin_inset Formula $30\,\text{kV/cm}$
\end_inset
 in air.
\end_layout

