). Although the cloud moves only 
\begin_inset Formula $0.15\,\text{mm}$
\end_inset
 by then, the drift brings the second streamer forward by about 
\begin_inset Formula $0.3\,\mu\text{s}$
\end_inset
. The criterion uses the tip field only; the stricter ionization integral along the axis, 
\begin_inset Formula $\int\left(\alpha-\eta\right)dz\ge K$
\end_inset
, would also account for how the space charge flattens the field in front of the tip. The second streamer itself is not modelled.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Figures 6 to 8: What the Paper Leaves Out
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Figures 6, 7 and 8 of [1] plot the inception voltage 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{cs}$
\end_inset
, the length 
\begin_inset Formula $L_{cs}$
\end_inset
 and the charge 
\begin_inset Formula $Q_{cs}$
\end_inset
 of the first and second corona streamers against the front time 
\begin_inset Formula $T_{f}$
\end_inset
 of the impulse (
\begin_inset Formula $15$
\end_inset
 to 
\begin_inset Formula $600\,\mu\text{s}$
\end_inset
, gaps of 
\begin_inset Formula $40$
\end_inset
 and 
\begin_inset Formula $80\,\text{cm}$
\end_inset
). Each point is a separate impulse. All three quantities fall as 
\begin_inset Formula $T_{f}$
\end_inset
 increases, and the second streamer always needs a higher voltage than the first.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The fall of 
\begin_inset Formula $V_{cs}$
\end_inset
 is the time-lag effect of inception: after the tip field exceeds its static threshold, a free electron must appear near the tip and the avalanche must grow into a streamer. On a fast front the voltage rises further during this delay. A higher inception voltage gives a stronger field further from the tip, hence a longer streamer with more charge.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In Figures 3 to 5 the inception voltage and the streamer length were 
\series bold
inputs
\series default
; in Figures 6 to 8 they are 
\series bold
outputs
\series default
, and the rules that produce them are not given. The paper refers to an earlier paper of the same authors, in Chinese, for these models. What is missing, and a candidate model from the literature on long air gaps for each item, is listed in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "tab:repro_missing"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"
tuple "list"

\end_inset
.
\end_layout

